Try with Resources
❑Programmers sometimes forget to close the files.
❑The Java language provides the try-with-resources syntax 
that automatically closes the open files:
try (declare and create resources) {
  Use the resource to process the file;
}
❑Using the try-with-resources syntax, we can rewrite the code 
as shown in the next slide.

